# Constant names currently declared in BOTH Rust and Lean.
#
# ⚠ THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. Every line is a rule written twice, which is a
# silent divergence waiting to happen: change one side, forget the other, and
# nothing says so. They are grandfathered because they predate the check, not
# because they are acceptable.
#
# A new entry needs a REASON on the line above it, and "it was easier" is not
# one. The usual right answers are: delete the Rust copy and ask Lean, or
# rename, if the two genuinely mean different things.
#
# Checked by scripts/rules-live-in-lean.sh. Measured 2026-09-12: 14 shared, of
# which ACCURACY_CEILING_M was the same name for two DIFFERENT rules (200.0 in
# Rust, 80 in Lean) and was renamed rather than listed.

# Calendar arithmetic. Genuinely constants of the world rather than decisions,
# but still two declarations that could disagree.
HOUR_BUCKETS
MINUTES_PER_DAY
METERS_PER_DEG_LAT

# Location-tail cache shape and freshness. Read by the route AND by the Lean
# cache rule, which is why both name them.
LATEST_FIX_TTL_MS
TAIL_MAX_POINTS
TAIL_TTL_MS

# Focus-place mining: how long asleep somewhere makes it a residence.
RESIDENCE_SLEEP_THRESHOLD_H
